{
	"info": {
		"name": "Customer Platform API",
		"_postman_id": "b1a2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-customerplatform",
		"description": "Colección de la Customer Management API (backend FastAPI) del proyecto customer-platform.\n\nAntes de usar: levanta el backend (`docker compose up --build` desde la raíz del repo, o `make dev-backend`). La variable `base_url` apunta por defecto a http://localhost:8000.\n\nToda respuesta de error comparte el envelope `{\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\", \"request_id\", \"details\"?}}`, y toda respuesta lleva `X-Request-ID`.\n\nImportable en Postman (Collection v2.1) e Insomnia.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "base_url",
			"value": "http://localhost:8000",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "customer_id",
			"value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Health",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
					"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
					"path": ["health"]
				},
				"description": "Comprobación de vida. Devuelve exactamente `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` y no toca la base de datos."
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
							"pm.test(\"cuerpo exacto\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: \"ok\" }));",
							"pm.test(\"llega X-Request-ID\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"x-request-id\")).to.be.a(\"string\"));"
						]
					}
				}
			],
			"response": [
				{
					"name": "200 ok",
					"status": "OK",
					"code": 200,
					"body": "{\n  \"status\": \"ok\"\n}"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Customers",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Crear cliente",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Sofía Navarro\",\n  \"email\": \"sofia.navarro@example.com\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers"]
						},
						"description": "`201` con el cliente creado. El estado inicial siempre es `PENDING`, aunque el body traiga otra cosa (el body solo acepta `name` y `email`). Un email que ya existe (incluso con otras mayúsculas) responde `409` con `EMAIL_ALREADY_EXISTS`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const code = pm.response.code;",
									"pm.test(\"201 o 409\", () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(code));",
									"if (code === 201) {",
									"  const body = pm.response.json();",
									"  pm.test(\"nace PENDING\", () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(\"PENDING\"));",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"customer_id\", body.id);",
									"  console.log(\"customer_id guardado:\", body.id);",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "201 creado",
							"status": "Created",
							"code": 201,
							"body": "{\n  \"id\": \"e56ec016-7746-4510-8295-d1af66714048\",\n  \"name\": \"Sofía Navarro\",\n  \"email\": \"sofia.navarro@example.com\",\n  \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-11-27T20:54:40.569009Z\"\n}"
						},
						{
							"name": "409 duplicado",
							"status": "Conflict",
							"code": 409,
							"body": "{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"EMAIL_ALREADY_EXISTS\",\n    \"message\": \"A customer with this email already exists.\",\n    \"request_id\": \"9213566a5b1d48cbad7ed5f03272ee92\"\n  }\n}"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Listar clientes",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers"]
						},
						"description": "`200` con un array plano ordenado por `created_at` descendente (desempate por `id`). Sin datos: `[]`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"200 y array\", () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an(\"array\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Listar filtrando por estado",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers?status=ACTIVE",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers"],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "status",
									"value": "ACTIVE",
									"description": "ACTIVE, PENDING o BLOCKED. Cualquier otro valor: 422."
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "Misma respuesta que el listado, solo con el estado pedido. Un `status` inválido responde `422` con `VALIDATION_ERROR`."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Consultar un cliente",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers/{{customer_id}}",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers", "{{customer_id}}"]
						},
						"description": "`200` con el cliente. Usa la variable `customer_id` (se guarda sola al crear uno con esta colección). Un id inexistente responde `404` con `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`; un id mal formado, `422`."
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "200 encontrado",
							"status": "OK",
							"code": 200,
							"body": "{\n  \"id\": \"36310aa0-bcc8-4668-8fcc-0969a389383a\",\n  \"name\": \"Carlos López\",\n  \"email\": \"carlos.lopez@example.com\",\n  \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T20:54:37.246901Z\"\n}"
						},
						{
							"name": "404 no existe",
							"status": "Not Found",
							"code": 404,
							"body": "{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND\",\n    \"message\": \"Customer not found.\",\n    \"request_id\": \"1619697fe7c646fe8c4f7863a87737c9\"\n  }\n}"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Cambiar el estado",
					"request": {
						"method": "PATCH",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers/{{customer_id}}/status",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers", "{{customer_id}}", "status"]
						},
						"description": "`200` con el cliente actualizado. Idempotente: repetir el mismo estado devuelve `200` igual. Un `status` fuera de `ACTIVE|PENDING|BLOCKED` responde `422` con el detalle por campo; un id inexistente, `404`."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"200 y estado aplicado\", () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ACTIVE\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "200 actualizado",
							"status": "OK",
							"code": 200,
							"body": "{\n  \"id\": \"36310aa0-bcc8-4668-8fcc-0969a389383a\",\n  \"name\": \"Carlos López\",\n  \"email\": \"carlos.lopez@example.com\",\n  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T20:54:37.246901Z\"\n}"
						},
						{
							"name": "422 estado inválido",
							"status": "Unprocessable Entity",
							"code": 422,
							"body": "{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n    \"message\": \"Invalid request.\",\n    \"request_id\": \"7a87a7bd083a4f83a5363870b8368e4f\",\n    \"details\": [\n      {\n        \"field\": \"status\",\n        \"message\": \"Input should be 'ACTIVE', 'PENDING' or 'BLOCKED'\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Errores (ejemplos)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "422 email inválido",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"X\",\n  \"email\": \"not-an-email\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers"]
						},
						"description": "Validación de Pydantic con el envelope unificado: `details` lista cada campo fallido."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"422 con code y details\", () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
									"  const err = pm.response.json().error;",
									"  pm.expect(err.code).to.eql(\"VALIDATION_ERROR\");",
									"  pm.expect(err.details[0].field).to.eql(\"email\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "404 id inexistente",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/customers/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["customers", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
						},
						"description": "Uuid bien formado que no existe en la base."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"404 con CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND\", () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql(\"CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "X-Request-ID eco",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "X-Request-ID",
								"value": "mi-trace-123"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["health"]
						},
						"description": "Si la petición trae un `X-Request-ID` válido, la respuesta lo reutiliza; si trae uno inválido (más de 128 caracteres o caracteres fuera de `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), se genera uno nuevo y el inválido no se devuelve. Ese mismo id va en los errores y en el log."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"el id enviado se reutiliza\", () => {",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"x-request-id\")).to.eql(\"mi-trace-123\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
